{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_MW0bKJJF2v8iP4Pecjm05053","content":"== graph_build.py\n\"\"\"Build the sensor graph from road distances, and check it before training.\n\nFollows gen_adj_mx.py of the DCRNN repository (Li et al. 2018), without reading its pickle.\n\n  distance_adjacency(rows, ids, k=0.1)  W_ij = exp(-(d_ij / sd)^2) for the directed distances given in rows\n                                        (from_id, to_id, distance); sd is the std of the finite distances;\n                                        weights below k become 0. Pairs not in rows stay 0\n  random_walk(w)                        D_out^-1 W; rows of nodes without out-edges stay 0\n  diffusion_supports(w)                 [P_f^T, P_b^T] with P_f = random_walk(w), P_b = random_walk(w^T),\n                                        the forward and backward supports of the diffusion convolution\n  graph_summary(w)                      nodes, directed edges without the diagonal, nodes with no in-edge,\n                                        no out-edge, no edge at all, weak components and the largest share\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef distance_adjacency(rows, ids, k=0.1):\n    pos = {int(s): i for i, s in enumerate(ids)}\n    d = np.full((len(ids), len(ids)), np.inf)\n    for a, b, dist in rows:\n        if int(a) in pos and int(b) in pos:\n            d[pos[int(a)], pos[int(b)]] = float(dist)\n    sd = d[np.isfinite(d)].std()\n    w = np.exp(-np.square(d / sd))\n    w[w < k] = 0.0\n    return w\n\n\ndef random_walk(w):\n    deg = w.sum(1)\n    inv = np.where(deg > 0, 1.0 / np.where(deg > 0, deg, 1.0), 0.0)\n    return inv[:, None] * w\n\n\ndef diffusion_supports(w):\n    return [random_walk(w).T, random_walk(w.T).T]\n\n\ndef graph_summary(w):\n== forecast_eval.py\n\"\"\"Windows, splits, baselines and paired evaluation for forecasting values on a sensor graph.\n\nFollows generate_training_data.py of the DCRNN repository. values is (time, nodes); 0 marks a missing reading.\n\n  window_starts(n_time, n_in, n_out)   sample t uses times t-n_in+1..t as input and t+1..t+n_out as output\n  split_counts(n)                       70% train, 20% test (rounded), the rest validation, in time order\n  make_xy(values, tod, starts, ...)     x (b, n_in, nodes, 2) = value and time in day; y (b, horizon, nodes)\n  time_in_day(t_ns)                     the fraction of the day of int64 nanoseconds\n  last_value(values, starts)            the last input value as the forecast for every horizon\n  historical_average(values, target, steps_per_week, weeks)\n                                        mean of the same time of the week over the previous weeks, zeros left out\n  masked_metrics(pred, truth)           MAE, RMSE, MAPE leaving out the points whose truth is 0\n  paired_day_sums(a, b, truth, days)    per day, sum of |a - truth| - |b - truth| and the count of kept points\n  day_sums(pred, truth, days)           per day, sum of |pred - truth| and the count (for one model's interval)\n  boot_ratio(sums, counts)              95% interval of sum / count, drawing whole days with replacement\n  share_of_gain(a, b, truth, mask)      the share of the total paired gain sum(|a|-|b|) that falls in mask\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef time_in_day(t_ns):\n    day = 86400 * 10**9\n    return (np.asarray(t_ns, dtype=\"int64\") % day) / day\n\n\ndef window_starts(n_time, n_in=12, n_out=12):\n    return np.arange(n_in - 1, n_time - n_out)\n\n\ndef split_counts(n):\n    test = round(n * 0.2)\n    train = round(n * 0.7)\n    return train, n - train - test, test\n\n\ndef make_xy(values, tod, starts, n_in=12, horizon=12):\n    xi = starts[:, None] + np.arange(-(n_in - 1), 1)[None, :]\n    yi = starts[:, None] + np.arange(1, horizon + 1)[None, :]\n    v = values[xi]\n== dcrnn.py\n\"\"\"DCRNN (Li et al. 2018) in PyTorch, with the pieces of its training loop.\n\nDiffusion convolution inside a GRU; an encoder over the inputs and a decoder over the horizon with scheduled\nsampling. k = 0 drops the graph: every node runs the same GRU and sees no neighbour (the ablation that\nmeasures what the graph adds).\n\n  DiffusionConv(supports, in_dim, out_dim, k)   [x, S x, T2 x, ..., per support] -> linear; T_k = 2 S T_{k-1} - T_{k-2}\n  DCGRUCell                                     GRU gates and candidate from diffusion convolutions\n  DCRNN(supports, num_nodes, in_dim, units, layers, k, horizon)\n     forward(x, y=None, teacher_prob=0)         x (b, n_in, n, in_dim) -> (b, horizon, n); y: the scaled truth,\n                                                fed to the decoder with probability teacher_prob while training\n  teacher_prob(step, tau=2000)                  tau / (tau + exp(step / tau)), the inverse sigmoid decay\n  masked_mae(pred, truth)                       mean |pred - truth| over the points whose truth is not 0\n  supports_to_torch(mats, device)               numpy supports (from graph_build.diffusion_supports) to tensors\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport torch\nfrom torch import nn\nclass DiffusionConv(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, supports, in_dim, out_dim, k, bias_start=0.0):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.supports, self.k = supports, k\n        n_mat = len(supports) * k + 1\n        self.lin = nn.Linear(in_dim * n_mat, out_dim)\n        nn.init.xavier_normal_(self.lin.weight)\n        nn.init.constant_(self.lin.bias, bias_start)\n\n    def forward(self, x):                      # x (b, n, d)\n        out = [x]\n        if self.k > 0:\n            for s in self.supports:\n                x1 = torch.einsum(\"ij,bjd->bid\", s, x)\n                out.append(x1)\n                x0 = x\n                for _ in range(2, self.k + 1):\n                    x2 = 2 * torch.einsum(\"ij,bjd->bid\", s, x1) - x0\n                    out.append(x2)\n                    x0, x1 = x1, x2"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"406cae65-a8b5-47c6-a918-803daf0c3a64","uuid":"3